{
  "about": [
    "Which lakes and rivers go on the Earth map. Read by scripts/build-earth-map.ts (npm run build:map).",
    "Shapes come from Natural Earth 1:50m (ne_50m_lakes, ne_50m_rivers_lake_centerlines).",
    "lakes: every natural lake (kind 'Lake' or 'Alkaline Lake', not reservoirs) of at least minAreaKm2,",
    "  plus the names in alsoInclude, minus the names in exclude. Names are Natural Earth's 'name' field.",
    "rivers: one entry per river. parts = the Natural Earth names of its pieces (big rivers are split into",
    "  pieces with local names, e.g. the Yangtze's upper course is 'Jinsha'). bbox [west, south, east, north]",
    "  keeps only pieces inside that box, for names used by two rivers (there's also a Colorado in Argentina).",
    "  dropLines leaves out the pieces that start or end at one of these [lon, lat] points (e.g. side branches of a delta).",
    "  extraLines adds hand-drawn lines as [[lon, lat], ...], for stretches Natural Earth doesn't have (or that its",
    "  coastline turns into specks of water, like the Amazon and St. Lawrence estuaries).",
    "A river whose mouth stops short of the sea, a big lake or another river is joined to the nearest one automatically."
  ],
  "lakes": {
    "minAreaKm2": 5000,
    "kinds": ["Lake", "Alkaline Lake"],
    "alsoInclude": ["North Aral Sea", "South Aral Sea"],
    "exclude": ["Lake Eyre North", "Lake Torrens"]
  },
